WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.860
- I know this is getting
lost in the shuffle

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.390
of all the crazy things that are happening

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.310
in the wake of the Capitol riots,

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.350
but it's important to not
lose sight of the fact

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:10.860
that President Trump committed
another impeachable offense

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.530
with respect to the
Georgia election results.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:15.900
We learned recently that
one of the U.S. attorneys

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:17.100
for one of the federal districts

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:20.130
in Georgia resigned amid pressure

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:23.610
from President Trump to
find more election fraud.

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:25.800
Byung J. Pak, who was the U.S. attorney

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.620
for one of the federal districts resigned

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:29.970
rather than comply with
the President's pressure

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.760
to engage in election fraud.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.210
Now I've already called
the totally improper call

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:36.100
between President Trump

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.520
and Secretary of State Brad Raffensperger,

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.870
but this alone in and of itself

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:44.840
is also just as bad and
just as impeachable.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:47.520
So let's not lose sight of that as well.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.590
Stay tuned for more
legal election coverage,

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.753
and as always, I'll see you in court.

